  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows strong bearish signals.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — apply a lag correction to prevent overshoot after sharp upward moves.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 10-day average, reduce by 5–10% to align with historical volatility.",
    "When sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0), allow slightly higher forecast bias to capture momentum, but cap at +15% above recent high.",
    "For long-term horizons (>14 days), reduce forecast volatility by 10–15% to reflect diminishing momentum and increased uncertainty.",
    "If true outcome consistently underperforms forecast (e.g., >10% error over 30d), apply a downward bias correction of 3–5% to avoid overconfidence in model."
